-- 목적: book_text 페이지 단위 본문 적재 (asb · 이 파일: 9of11)
-- 실행자: 팀장(Supabase SQL Editor). 워커 초안. 워커 DB 직접 쓰기 금지.
-- 근거 ADR: ADR-0056 (ADR-0056 D1·D2·D4·D5) · Accepted 2026-08-10
-- source 라벨: manifest_txt_v1
-- 이 파일 담당: 48권 / 465행 (정제 후 빈 면 0행 포함 — D7)
-- 생성기: scripts/tts_pilot/gen_book_text_sql_v2.py
-- 매핑: page_index = (P번호|json page) - 1 (0-based, D2/D11). blocks = NULL(원천에 블록 정보 없음).
-- 정제: tts_targets.sanitize() 공유(D6). 표지 행 없음(D3).
-- 인용: $$ 달러 인용. 생성 시 '$$' 포함·'$' 종결 전수 가드 통과.
-- 중복: ON CONFLICT (book_id, page_index) DO NOTHING — 기존 행을 덮어쓰지 않는다.
--
-- ★ 이 파일은 ROLLBACK; 으로 끝난다. [적재검증]까지 기대값과 일치하면
--   마지막 ROLLBACK; 을 COMMIT; 으로 직접 바꿔 타이핑해 확정한다.

-- ───────── [선검증] 트랜잭션 밖 ─────────
-- (a) 대상 권의 기존 book_text 행 수 — 기대 0. 0이 아니면 중단하고 보고할 것.
SELECT count(*) AS rows_before FROM book_text bt
  JOIN books b ON b.id = bt.book_id
  WHERE b.source_platform='african_storybook' AND b.source_id IN ('36851', '36888', '36895', '36897', '36898', '36899', '36904', '36908', '36909', '36912', '36914', '36918', '36926', '36927', '36931', '36933', '36945', '36987', '36993', '36998', '37009', '37033', '37036', '37096', '37129', '37137', '37155', '37186', '37208', '37218', '37281', '37309', '37311', '37350', '37352', '37353', '37385', '37457', '37488', '37496', '37501', '37515', '37541', '37552', '37559', '37579', '37629', '37753');
-- (b) 대상 source_id 중 books에 존재하는 권 수 — 기대 48
SELECT count(*) AS books_found FROM books
  WHERE source_platform='african_storybook' AND source_id IN ('36851', '36888', '36895', '36897', '36898', '36899', '36904', '36908', '36909', '36912', '36914', '36918', '36926', '36927', '36931', '36933', '36945', '36987', '36993', '36998', '37009', '37033', '37036', '37096', '37129', '37137', '37155', '37186', '37208', '37218', '37281', '37309', '37311', '37350', '37352', '37353', '37385', '37457', '37488', '37496', '37501', '37515', '37541', '37552', '37559', '37579', '37629', '37753');

-- ───────── [적재] ─────────
BEGIN;
INSERT INTO book_text (book_id, page_index, text, blocks, source)
SELECT b.id, v.page_index, v.text, NULL::jsonb, $$manifest_txt_v1$$
  FROM (VALUES
    ('36851', 0, $$Once apon a time a kingdom named gaffer was a new one. One day the king wanted to burn half of the land for a big palace.$$),
    ('36851', 1, $$The people shouted you can build a home fore your self but not us. The people went away and the kingdom was infamous and called the kingdom of dispose.$$),
    ('36851', 2, $$Many years later a boy named Dave thoute a person will go to the king and demand the throne.$$),
    ('36851', 3, $$In the third day on the 9th month of the year Dave's baby brother was born.$$),
    ('36851', 4, $$His name was Mosley and when he grew up he became a hunter.$$),
    ('36851', 5, $$A little boy said go and hunt the king and he agreed.$$),
    ('36851', 6, $$He went to the palace and threw a arrow in his heart and became a good king the end.$$),
    ('36888', 0, $$There once was a girl by the name of Thembi, she lived with mother in a small village. They were very poor and hardly had any food to eat everyday. This made her mother very sad. Every night before bed, her mother would kneel down and pray, asking GOD to create a better and successful life for her daughter.$$),
    ('36888', 1, $$Thembi is at school. She loves learning new things. She likes, reading books and helping others. When Thembi grows up, she would like to become a Doctor.$$),
    ('36888', 2, $$Everyday Thembi walks to school and her mother is out looking for a job. After walking around for hours hungry and thirsty her mom meets an old man, in need of a domestic worker.$$),
    ('36888', 3, $$Thembi's mom speaks to the old man, telling him how she needs a job and he needs the help. With a big smile on the old mans face he offers her the job.$$),
    ('36888', 4, $$She couldn't wait for Thembi to get home, so she can tell her the great news that she found a job today and they don't have to worry about food anymore.$$),
    ('36888', 5, $$Thembi's mom woke up early the next morning and off they went, Thembi went to school and her mom went to work. She did the man's washing, washed the dishes, ironed his clothes and scrubbed the floors. The old man was impressed by all the work she managed to do in one day. He then paid her and she went home very happy.$$),
    ('36888', 6, $$She used her money very wisely, she bought food and a few seeds which she planted as soon as she got home. A few months had passed and before they knew there were some fruit and vegetables growing in their own back yard. Thembi's mom would sell the fruit and vegetables and all the money she had made she would bank so that Thembelihle could go to varsity one day.$$),
    ('36888', 7, $$Finally the day arrived for Thembi to start varsity which she did, Thembi went on and became a successful doctor and she made tons of money. Thembi opened a spaza shop for her mom where she sold more than fruit and vegetables. They also made regular donations to orphanages.$$),
    ('36888', 8, $$Thembi was so greatful to GOD for all that HE has done for them that she wrote a song in adoration to GOD. THE SONG: Thank you heavenly father, I'm eternally greatful for all your blessings, YOU haven't failed me yet, OH LORD you're faithful, OH LORD you're faithful, YOU haven't failed me yet!!$$),
    ('36895', 0, $$My name is Kaydin Vanere, I was born on the 15 of October 2009. My family and I lived in Klipspruit Ext 10. My brother and I loved playing soccer outside in the yard. My mother was always in the kitchen baking or cooking that's her favourite things to do. My dad was always fixing things around the house, I remember mom saying we so lucky to have our own handyman.$$),
    ('36895', 1, $$When I was about five years old sadly our family home in Ext 10 Klipspruit burned down with all our valuables, everything we owned burnt to ashes that was one of the saddest days for my family.$$),
    ('36895', 2, $$We now live next to my grandmother in Kliptown. This was a big adjustment for all of us, my brother couldn't sleep at night because his favourite teddy burnt that day, so most of the night he would cry. My mom and dad were sad too, but eventually we all settled in and we much happier.$$),
    ('36895', 3, $$I turned 6 and everyday I cried when my mom dropped me off at crèche, going to crèche wasn't one of my favourite things to do because they made me read and reading wasn't much fun for me. I couldn't wait to start school.$$),
    ('36895', 4, $$Finally my first day at school, I was super excited, little did I know that I would do a whole lot more reading. I dreaded going to school because the other kids would laugh at me when I read, I really struggled.$$),
    ('36895', 5, $$My mom enrolled me at a centre called GIVERS. Everyday after school I would go there. The teachers at this centre were the most helpful, caring people I've ever met. They helped me with my homework daily and they taught me how to read, I never thought I would ever enjoy reading until the teachers at the centre helped me and showed me that reading could be fun.$$),
    ('36895', 6, $$Reading now is one of my favourite things to do. I'm no longer shy to read in class at school, the other kids no longer laugh at me. Learning is fun.$$),
    ('36895', 7, $$The centre also has many other programmes that they run and one of them is called Simunye College. Simunye College had a competition for a book fest, each one of us had to write our very own story. I took part in the competition, sadly I never won. A girl from the centre by the Faith won the competition.$$),
    ('36895', 8, $$Our teachers at the centre told us that no matter what we are all winners. They also said that we should never give up, to always try our best in whatever we do. Even though I never won the competition it motivated me to continue reading and trying even harder at writing.$$),
    ('36895', 9, $$Simunye College and the teachers at the centre taught us a lot and personally they helped me a whole lot, without them I would never have written my very own story. I would like to say thank you to all the teachers at the centre for teaching us how to write our own stories.$$),
    ('36895', 10, $$I really like writing now and writing my own stories is so much fun. As soon as I complete school I would love to pursue my dream and become a successful writer all thanks to my teachers at the centre and Simunye College.$$),
    ('36897', 0, $$There is an NGO that goes by the name P. U. S. H which stands for… P – Persevere@U – Until@S – Something@H – Happens$$),
    ('36897', 1, $$After school many kids go to PUSH where we all get food, we are assisted with homework, after eating and homework we play lots of fun games with the teachers at the centre. I have a lot of friends at the centre and that's where I met my best friend Jayden.$$),
    ('36897', 2, $$Before Jayden and I became friends Jayden was an angry boy, he always fought with the other kids and when he wasn't fighting he would tease the other kids. None of the kids liked playing with Jayden.$$),
    ('36897', 3, $$The owner of PUSH Mam Lorna heard Jayden being nasty to the other kids and how he was teasing them, she called him and said my child don't be nasty it's not very nice to tease the other children.$$),
    ('36897', 4, $$Why are you being mean to them? Jayden looked at her and said Mam Lorna I don't have any friends here none of these kids want to play with me.$$),
    ('36897', 5, $$Mam Lorna gave him a hug and said my boy if you are friendlier to the other kids and stop teasing them they would play with you.$$),
    ('36897', 6, $$A few weeks later was Jayden's birthday as he walked in the centre he saw a big balloon with his name on it and the place was decorated and as he got closer he saw a cake with his name on it too, finally when he was close enough everyone there started singing happy birthday to him.$$),
    ('36897', 7, $$Jayden couldn't believe his eyes nor could he stop smiling, Mam Lorna then said to him here at PUSH we all LOVE one another and we all care for one another. We all love and care for you.$$),
    ('36897', 8, $$Jayden was still in shock by what he saw and heard the boy couldn't utter a word he just started crying. Everyone wished him a happy birthday. This made Jayden very happy, we played had cake and everyone had a good time.$$),
    ('36897', 9, $$The next day Jayden came to the centre a totally different kid, he didn't teased anyone nor was he being mean to anyone. Jayden is much happier at PUSH and now he has a lot of friends.$$),
    ('36898', 0, $$Sipho: Yo mom my day was great!! @Mom do you remember I had a math test.@Mom: yes@Sipho: I passed!$$),
    ('36898', 1, $$Mom: I'm so proud of you my baby.@Sipho: Our school principal asked me to participate in the spelling bee competition at school.$$),
    ('36898', 2, $$Mom: That's great, you better start studying now if you want to win.$$),
    ('36898', 3, $$Mom: Why are you up so early?@Sipho: Fueling up my system before our spelling bee competition.@Mom: Good luck my baby.$$),
    ('36898', 4, $$The following day was the competition, all the kids at school was excited. I heard Sipho say a praying asking God to make him win the competition.$$),
    ('36898', 5, $$Everyone who participated could not wait to receive the results, however the results. We were all buzzing with excitement.$$),
    ('36898', 6, $$The results were finally out, and all the participants were hoping that they would win, finally the winner was announced…@And the winner is Sipho!!$$),
    ('36898', 7, $$I couldn't stop screaming yeah I won!! I ran home as fast as I could, I couldn't wait a minute longer I just need to tell mom.$$),
    ('36898', 8, $$Sipho: Mom, mom!! I won, I won!!@Mom: Whoa slow down, what are you saying?@Sipho: Well mom remember the recycling competition? The competition results came out today.$$),
    ('36898', 9, $$Sipho: I won, just like I said I would.@Mom: I knew you'd you win.$$),
    ('36899', 0, $$Layla was only six years old when she started helping her mother in the garden.$$),
    ('36899', 1, $$Together they planted different vegetables and flowers. Their garden had carrots, green beans, potatoes, tomatoes, onions and beautiful flowers.$$),
    ('36899', 2, $$Layla loved helping her mother in the garden and more so she loved playing with water.$$),
    ('36899', 3, $$When Layla isn't helping her mom in the garden, she is playing with her friends.$$),
    ('36899', 4, $$They sold vegetables in the neighbourhood and with the money they made they were able to but groceries.$$),
    ('36899', 5, $$Her brother and sister go to school using the money that they make from selling vegetables.$$),
    ('36899', 6, $$Layla asked her mother if they could open a market and her mother said that, that was a good idea.$$),
    ('36899', 7, $$It's always been Layla's dream to own her very own market, or even become one of the biggest suppliers nationwide.$$),
    ('36899', 8, $$Layla would love to buy her mother and siblings a big house so can all live comfortably.$$),
    ('36899', 9, $$With a lot of hard work, planting and a whole lot more ploughing, Layla's dream became a reality. She supplied all the small markets with fruit and vegetables, Layla bought her mother and siblings a big house and they all lived happily ever after.$$),
    ('36904', 0, $$Good morning mom, good morning dad. Paul and Kim Dent are up in a good time this morning. School begins today. It's the end of the holiday. They enjoy having holidays and the enjoy school too. Have your breakfast now, says Mrs Dent to Paul and Kim. Dad is having his breakfast, He is in a hurry this morning. You need to hurry too.$$),
    ('36904', 1, $$You are going to school by bus, I'm sorry you cannot go by car this morning, say Mr Dent, but I must be off by seven o'clock. I like to ride in the bus, says Kim. So do I, says Paul. I like to sit by the window. I like to ring the bell at the bus stop, says Kim. Mr Dent puts on his jacket. The key of the car is in his pocket. Well, he says, it's a nice sunny morning. Have a happy day at school. Goodbye. Goodbye dad.$$),
    ('36904', 2, $$Is it time to get ready now? Kim looks at the clock. Yes it is, says Mrs Dent. I can dress myself, say Kim. So can I, say Paul. They run to get ready for school. Kim puts on her school dress. It has a pocket and a belt. She puts on her white socks and black shoes. The white socks are new. They are a present from her gran. Do you have a handkerchief Kim? Asks her mother. Yes thank you mom, say Kim. It's in the pocket of my dress.$$),
    ('36904', 3, $$Paul puts on his school shirt and socks. He has a belt and shorts. He puts on his grey socks and black shoes. His grey socks are new too. They are a present from gran. I must not forget my handkerchief, he says. I left one out for you says his mother. Here it is. You must put it in your shirts pocket, or it will get lost. Now you must pack your school bags, are they ready for school?$$),
    ('36904', 4, $$My school bag is ready, says Paul. Look here's my pencil. Here's my book. My crayons are in this pocket. My pencil, crayons and book is in my bag too, says Kim. Mrs Dent comes from the kitchen, here's your lunch boxes, she says. Do you want an apple or some figs with your lunch? Oh an apple, says Paul. Some figs for me please, says Kim, some nice soft figs. She and Paul put their lunch boxes in their school bags.$$),
    ('36904', 5, $$Come now says Mrs Dent. It is time to go to the bus stop. You must not miss the bus. Kim puts on her hat. It has a band and badge on it. Paul puts on his grey cap. It has a badge on it too. They carry their school bags. You look smart, says Mrs Dent, as she waves goodbye.$$),
    ('36904', 6, $$Look, Hilton is at the bus stop. He is going to school for the first time. His mother is with him. Hilton looks very smart in his new shirt and pants. His socks, shoes, cap with the badge are all new as well. Good morning Mrs Mills, says Kim. Hello Hilton, says Paul. Are you glad you going to school for the first time? Oh yes, says Hilton. This is my new school bag, granny sent it to me. I can lock it with this little key.$$),
    ('36904', 7, $$Did you have a good holiday? Asks Mrs Mills. Yes we did, says Kim. We went on a camp, we had a tent with us. We had lots of fun. Yes, says Paul. A camping holiday is fun. I want to go camping for the next holiday too. What did you do Hilton? We had a lot of fun too, says Hilton. We went on an airplane to see granny. It went high and very fast. It went up in the clouds. I have a picture of it. Here it is. Look at it's big tail.$$),
    ('36904', 8, $$Look here comes the bus, says Mrs Mills. In we go. Paul, Kim and Hilton sit at the back window. They like sitting there. What a lot there is to see on the bus ride to school. A lorry and a van go by. Lots of cars go by. There is Jeff. He is getting a lift in this dad's car. There is Sally. She is going along with her brother and sister. Watch Kim, says Paul. Hurry it's time to ring the bell now. We must get out at the next stop.$$),
    ('36904', 9, $$Look mom, there is the school, says Hilton. It is a very big school. Yes, says Mrs Mills, what a lot of boys and girls there are. Come let's go in, we're just in time. The End$$),
    ('36908', 0, $$It was a sunny day and Kira was playing outside with her friends. Her parents called her in the house to tell her to babysit the neighbours twin babies,because we are going with them to a vacation for today and Kira was excited.$$),
    ('36908', 1, $$Dad also allowed her to invite her best friend, and Nancy was already there ready to help. Kira's parents were off and they were left with the baby twins Ryan and Bryan they were cute baby boys, suddenly the babies began to cry.$$),
    ('36908', 2, $$Kira decided to go and make a bottle of milk for the babies while Nancy looked after the babies. On the way downstairs Kira heard the door shutting, she got scared and she ran upstairs. Kira asked Nancy if she left the door opened.$$),
    ('36908', 3, $$Suprised to know she closed the door, they thought there was a monster. The children fell asleep. Night fall came and they ordered pizza when they went to collect the pizza it had a picture of a pumpkin with eyes the girls got frightened.$$),
    ('36908', 4, $$The babies woke up and they ate pizza when they finished eating the lights went on and off. They were shaken they went to watch their favourite TV show. The lights suddenly went off they switched on the torch.$$),
    ('36908', 5, $$Pointing at a direction they saw a figure standing with a white cloth covering the body and it said "Bhoo" the children got scared. The light got switched and the figure removed the cloth covering the body and guess who it was it was DAD!$$),
    ('36908', 6, $$He laughed and they all started to laugh even the neighbours and mum started to laugh. Kira was no longer interested in babysitting because she wouldn't be able to deal with a spooking crisis again, but she really enjoyed.$$),
    ('36909', 0, $$Once upon a time there were four children Sam,Lucas,Pearl and Lydia. They were best friends they cared for each other they liked reading comic books but they loved reading fictional stories the most.$$),
    ('36909', 1, $$The children lived in a small town in Italy they went to a school called The Bees they were in seventh grade. One day after school the children went to the library in the afternoon just after school. They came across a book called Mega Land.$$),
    ('36909', 2, $$The children sat down and started reading right after going through the second page time was up. The children began to fight they wanted to go home with the book but there was only one book for one person, so Lucas went home with it.$$),
    ('36909', 3, $$Lucas got home and changed his uniform,did his homework,ate dinner and washed the dishes. He had to miss his favourite show so that he could read his book Mega Land.$$),
    ('36909', 4, $$He read a lot about Mega Land evil robots that had took over the City and destroyed everything and a super hero who was betrayed and trapped in a cave by his best friend and could not stop the disaster. The book was a bit scary.$$),
    ('36909', 5, $$Mom said it is bed time and Lucas went to sleep,he closed his eyes and found himself at the park with Sam, Lydia and Pearl. They saw a tree house and opened the door and went in. Instead of going in the tree house they went to another place.$$),
    ('36909', 6, $$They were suddenly surrounded by robots robotic cities they were in Mega Land. A robot came to them and looked at them in suprise "human children" he said,I guess you read about the book Mega Land the robot offered to help save the city.$$),
    ('36909', 7, $$The children encountered against the gigantic robotic octopus which sprayed them with slime and mud and they fought with the Robot Pirate the most evil pirate. The children swam through the seven seas and battled with the sea creatures.$$),
    ('36909', 8, $$They reached the fort where the superhero was hidden they rescued the superhero and the superhero defeated all the evil robots. The superhero thanked the children and especially Lucas. Lucas woke up and got ready for school.$$),
    ('36909', 9, $$He shared his dream with his friends and they laughed at such ridiculousness, but he really dreamt about that.$$),
    ('36912', 0, $$My name is Enrica Smith, I'm the youngest of five kids. Being the youngest is so much fun, my older siblings often bully me and I don't like it. My dad usually shouts at them to leave me alone. They only listen for that time and the next day they at it again.$$),
    ('36912', 1, $$Even though I fight with them a lot, I know that when it comes to my wellbeing they always have my back. I don't like what they are doing but one thing I know for sure, is that they love me and I love them a lot.$$),
    ('36912', 2, $$My Dad is the pillar of my strength, my number one supporter. My dad introduced me to soccer, I'm our school's mid-fielder. I love playing soccer.$$),
    ('36912', 3, $$The fun side of being the youngest is that I get spoiled by our dad. After every match I play my dad buys me my favorite chocolate chip ice-cream and says, I shouldn't tell the others.$$),
    ('36912', 4, $$I love my dad he is always there when I need him and he makes sure that I'm always happy.$$),
    ('36912', 5, $$I was very young when my mom passed away and I really miss her. I wish she was still around to take me shopping, oh how I loved it when she bought me new things.$$),
    ('36912', 6, $$I only have a few memories of my mom and when my siblings speaks about her they tell me how much fun she was. She was extremely funny and always had a smile on her face.$$),
    ('36912', 7, $$I miss her more with each passing day, if only I had another day, to see that smile upon her face. I know she is my guardian angel in heaven. Mom I love you so much I wish you didn't have to leave. Dad says, one day mom and I will meet again and that brings me so much comfort knowing she will be waiting for me.$$),
    ('36912', 8, $$I love my family and I'm truly thankful for all their love and support and for helping dad when it comes to raising me.$$),
    ('36912', 9, $$The End.$$),
    ('36914', 0, $$In a village full of shacks and only one built with bricks. There lived a little boy named Nido.$$),
    ('36914', 1, $$Nido and his parents lived in a big house. The only brick house in our village. The rest of the village had small little shacks.$$),
    ('36914', 2, $$Nido was selfish and cruel. He would never play the games his friends wanted to play. So they always played games Nido liked.$$),
    ('36914', 3, $$Nido always had the best of everything in our village. He had the coolest toys, the latest technology and only wore name brand clothes. He would brag about what he had and made his friends feel bad for not having what he had.$$),
    ('36914', 4, $$Nido's mom and dad were always busy with work and they were hardly ever home. Nido would always invite friends over but they weren't allowed to touch or play with his toys.$$),
    ('36914', 5, $$This frustrated his friends because they were always sharing whatever they had with him and made him play with their toys.$$),
    ('36914', 6, $$Nido's friends left angry and rode off with their bicycles. This made Nido sad and angry because he was left all alone in a big empty house.$$),
    ('36914', 7, $$Nido's birthday was coming up and he was excited, his mom said he can invite as many friends as he wanted too. Nido then invited all of his friends and told them all the fun things they were going to do, they would have two jumping castles, a photo booth, a cotton candy machine, a pop-corn machine, a chocolate fountain and loads more.$$),
    ('36914', 8, $$Finally the day arrived, it's Nido's birthday. All the things were there just like Nido said it would be. Hours had passed and no one showed up for his birthday celebration. Nido went to his room and spent the rest of the day crying.$$),
    ('36914', 9, $$Nido asked his friends why none of them showed up for his birthday celebration and they told him that he was selfish and they weren't going to attend his party and watch him have fun all by himself. Nido then apologized to all of his friends and promised never to be selfish again.$$),
    ('36918', 0, $$Long ago, when the earth still lived in darkness, a young boy was born with an incredible power. His skin shined light on the earth. He was named Sun.$$),
    ('36918', 1, $$Soon, everyone in the village knew of his power and asked for his help. But he could not help everyone at once. The villagers grew angry.$$),
    ('36918', 2, $$Sun wanted peace. He looked to the sky and came up with a solution. Sun concentrated on the sky and slowly rose higher and higher.$$),
    ('36918', 3, $$The villagers watched Sun rise to the sky. As Sun rose, he brought light to the whole village. Everyone thanked him.$$),
    ('36918', 4, $$And so, Sun and the villagers came to an agreement. Sun would spend half the day in the sky and half with his family. In return, the villagers would never fight again.$$),
    ('36918', 5, $$And that is the story of a boy named Sun.$$),
    ('36926', 0, $$Once there was a girl named Natalie, she was also known as Naughty-Lee. She got the name Naughty-Lee as she was a very naughty little girl that never listened to her parents. Her parents mostly despised Natalie's attitude and mischievous tendencies.$$),
    ('36926', 1, $$Natalie was always up to mischief and evil ways, she never cared how she made anybody feel. While at school Naughty-Lee saw one of her classmates having her lunch, she than walked up to her demanded the girl to give her lunch over.$$),
    ('36926', 2, $$While all this was happening the teacher appeared and asked the girl what was happening, by than the teacher was already aware that Natalie was a bully. After the girl explained to the teacher what has just happened the teacher than reprimanded Natalie to go to the office immediately.$$),
    ('36926', 3, $$The teacher than arrived in the office together with Natalie. The teacher than asked Natalie to explain her side of the story and surprisingly for the first time Natalie spoke the truth about what has happened, she also added that she has an attitude problem and confessed to being a bully.$$),
    ('36926', 4, $$The teacher than spoke to Natalie saying: "imagine how you'd feel if people did the same thing to you. " She also advised that before Natalie does things to other people that she should always think, how she would feel first.$$),
    ('36926', 5, $$Few days later, Natalie decided to volunteer at her local old age home. Her duties at the old age home was to assist with beverages and food for the old people.$$),
    ('36926', 6, $$One day while tidying up Natalie came across the semi blind man from the road, Natalie than realized what a bad thing she has done so she built up courage and walked up to the old man saying: "I'm sorry for placing the rock in your way. " The old man replied: "afternoon my child, do you know that I could have been hurt badly as I am old and semi blind, however I do accept your apology. "$$),
    ('36926', 7, $$Later that day Natalie finished up than decided to take a walk home, as Natalie was walking home she admired the view of the beautiful sunset. Upon her arrival she asked forgiveness from her parents for being such a naughty little girl.$$),
    ('36926', 8, $$I am sorry for giving you so much trouble while growing up and having a bad attitude towards you. Her mother then responded: "I have been praying for this day! and the father added "I am very happy that you made a change in your behaviour, we love you and we forgive you. "$$),
    ('36926', 9, $$As time passed everyone Natalie has hurt in the past had forgiven her. Natalie then started making new friends and became a better person.$$),
    ('36927', 0, $$There was a boy by the name Jabu, Jabu lived a happy life with his parents and two sisters. They lived in a nice neighbourhood and went to the best schools. Jabu was the captain of his soccer team. He was a popular boy and everyone in school knew who he was. He enjoyed the attention.$$),
    ('36927', 1, $$His dad finally landed his dream job which meant that the family would live an even better life because they would have more money and it's the job that his father always wanted.$$),
    ('36927', 2, $$Everyone was excited for dad's new jobs except Jabu. Jabu knew that dad, getting his dream job would mean that they would have to relocate.$$),
    ('36927', 3, $$They eventually moved. Jabu and his siblings were all at the new school and Jabu hated every minute of it. Being the new kid wasn't fun at all for Jabu. After a month of their arrival, everything about Jabu changed, he no longer played soccer and hardly ever went out. Jabu hated school.$$),
    ('36927', 4, $$His father noticed a change in Jabu's behaviour, so he sat him down and they had a lengthy conversation and Jabu told him all about the bully at school.$$),
    ('36927', 5, $$The next day Jabu and his father spoke to the school principal regarding the student who is bullying kids, Jason the school bully was called into the principal's office along with his parents.$$),
    ('36927', 6, $$Jason was reprimanded and his parents seeked counselling for him. Jason apologised to Jabu and promised to be a better person. Since then no bullying ever took place at that school again, Jabu and Jason became best friends.$$),
    ('36931', 0, $$Long ago in Chadima Village, the sky was like a roof over the earth. It was so low, that the people could reach up and touch it. Their Gods lived inside the sky.$$),
    ('36931', 1, $$The sky was so low that the Gods could always hear the people's prayers, songs, and fights. When the people needed help, they would look up and speak to the Gods.$$),
    ('36931', 2, $$But the Gods had no rest. The people made noise all day and all night. They wiped their dirty hands on the clouds, making the home of the Gods dirty.$$),
    ('36931', 3, $$One day, after harvest time, all the women of Chadima came together and started pounding their corn in many, many mortars with long and heavy pounding sticks.$$),
    ('36931', 4, $$As the sticks were raised and lowered, the women poked and punched the sky. The Gods were hit and pushed. The women worked all day and all night, hurting the Gods.$$),
    ('36931', 5, $$The Gods had enough! They called a meeting fast and decided that the sky must be raised higher if they wanted to be safe from the pounding sticks of the women.$$),
    ('36931', 6, $$Quickly, they raised the sky so high that the women of the earth could not hurt them. And that is why the sky is so high today. The End.$$),
    ('36933', 0, $$Once there was a child who wandered the earth alone. She had no father or mother and was very sad.$$),
    ('36933', 1, $$Nobody paid attention to her. Her loneliness made her want to cry, but she did not know how to because tears did not exist in the world yet.$$),
    ('36933', 2, $$When the moon saw the child walking alone, he felt compassion. When the night came, the moon fell to the earth to meet the child.$$),
    ('36933', 3, $$The moon said, "Let go of your sorrow and cry! But do not let your tears stain the earth. Let your tears fall on me, and I will take them back to the sky. "$$),
    ('36933', 4, $$The orphan child wept the first tears into the world and they fell on the moon. The moon promised to look over her and went back to the sky.$$),
    ('36933', 5, $$From that day on the child was happy. Everyone in her village loved and protected her. She never cried again.$$),
    ('36933', 6, $$To this day, the moon holds the stains of the child's tears to remind us of the orphan child's sorrow.$$),
    ('36945', 0, $$My name is Cliche Wessels and i am 11 years of age. Ever since i started school i barely had any friends. I was more of a introvert and very dedicated to my school work.$$),
    ('36945', 1, $$Since the beginning of of my grade 6 year, I noticed a new girl in my class her name was Micheala.$$),
    ('36945', 2, $$From what I could pick up she was very smart, polite and friendly. Unlike me she was a extrovert.$$),
    ('36945', 3, $$Micheala always approached me asking how i´m doing?, after a few days it became a norm and soon after a how you was only a start of many other conversations.$$),
    ('36945', 4, $$Micheala told me about her family,where she comes from, her previous school and the friends that she had.$$),
    ('36945', 5, $$Micheala almost explained her whole life to me, from that i could pick up that she was from a very well off and wonderful family, that always supports her in everything that she does. Sometimes i wish i could have a family like that$$),
    ('36945', 6, $$As time passed me and Micheala became extremely close. We than started meeting each others family.$$),
    ('36945', 7, $$I started calling her my best friend as we started doing everything together,from homework to even church on Sundays.$$),
    ('36945', 8, $$I became so close to her that whatever happened in my life i could not wait to tell her the ¨tea¨.$$),
    ('36945', 9, $$I did not have any friends before, i always wondered why?, but now i know that God didn´t want to give m e just anyone because he had my best friend on her way and thank God for her daily.$$),
    ('36987', 0, $$I woke up early in the morning because we were going to Mombasa. I brushed my teeth and washed my face.$$),
    ('36987', 1, $$I went downstairs and ate my breakfast. Then,I went to the sitting room and watched television.$$),
    ('36987', 2, $$I went upstairs and packed my clothes,swimming costume,toys and camera.$$),
    ('36987', 3, $$I went downstairs and packed the food and water. I also brought a blanket so that I can sleep on the way.$$),
    ('36987', 4, $$We then carried the luggage to the car. We got in the car and started our journey.$$),
    ('36987', 5, $$When we were driving to Mombasa we saw many hills,mountains,bridges and cars.$$),
    ('36987', 6, $$When we got there, we saw two big elephant trunks crossed together.$$),
    ('36987', 7, $$We went to the beach and saw a camel and many people. We stayed there for 1hour and then I played with sand.$$),
    ('36987', 8, $$We went to a hotel and slept there for 1 day the hotel had a pool.$$),
    ('36987', 9, $$We went to fort Jesus we saw some old buildings. We saw many people.$$),
    ('36987', 10, $$And then we went to an old town in Mombasa. We saw many people and vehicles.$$),
    ('36987', 11, $$We went to Haller park we saw many animals like monkey, hippo and so many more$$),
    ('36987', 12, $$And then we went back home with an aeroplane. I slept in the plane because I was tired . THE END.$$),
    ('36993', 0, $$Me and mum are reading a book about rainbows I hope I see one, one day if I see one I will be so excited$$),
    ('36993', 1, $$It started raining hard for hours and the sun was out. After the rain I couldn’t believe my eyes there was a rainbow I jumped in joy. Then I said look mummy look mummy there is a rainbow!$$),
    ('36993', 2, $$We sat infront of the book looking at the rainbow. I was so exited to go to the park so I can see the rainbow better .$$),
    ('36993', 3, $$When we got to the park we sat down on the bench closer to the rainbow.$$),
    ('36993', 4, $$A few moments later there were five people looking at the rainbow like they knew that there will be a rainbow.$$),
    ('36993', 5, $$They looked at the rainbow like they have never seen one in a long time. But I hade so much fun. Hope you liked this story$$),
    ('36998', 0, $$On the edges of the Kafue River, was a small village called Kasupa. In this village, there lived a little girl and her grandmother. The girl's name was Lindiwe and she was a beautiful girl. Lindiwe lost her parents when she was just two months old. However, she was loved by her grandmother so much that she could not miss her parents. Her grandmother provided her with all she needed and Lindiwe's beauty was projected.$$),
    ('36998', 1, $$Lindiwe was called a super chocolate girl by many people because of her beauty. She was a dark brown beautiful girl, with long curly hair. She was lovely and talented with a very sweet and beautiful voice. Lindiwe loved singing and dancing, she also loved watching the sunset over the river while dancing to the African drum beat with her friends and family.$$),
    ('36998', 2, $$One bright morning, Lindiwe decided to visit the next village across the river. As she was about to leave the house happily singing, she saw a stranger talking with her grandmother. Lindiwe's grandmother sat her down and explained to her that the stranger thought she had an amazing voice and wanted her to participate in a talent search competition. @Lindiwe took part, won the competition and was given lots of money, a Gold Cup and was awarded a big singing contract.$$),
    ('36998', 3, $$The sweet voice which Lindiwe was talented with made her and her grandmother to leave Kafue banks and flew over to London. Lindiwe had only seen planes flying over her hut back at her village; she had never imagined that one day her grandmother and she would be privileged to fly. Her excitement superseded her; she jumped up and down as she boarded her flight. Eleven hours later, she disembarked at Heathrow Airport.$$),
    ('36998', 4, $$Her grandmother and she proceeded to board a tube which was a super fast train to London town. The two enjoyed the scenery as they cruised to the town centre. Lindiwe could not believe she was here, she was really here! It was as beautiful as she had always imagined. Their tube came to a halt at their station and her grandmother and she stepped out.$$),
    ('36998', 5, $$After staying in London for couple of years, Lindiwe and the grandmother decided that they should go back home, as the saying goes, "home is home though it may never be so homely". When they got back, they built a hotel where the village house used to be. The hotel had a lot of visitors as it was near the river. The hotel business was doing very well especially during holidays. Lindiwe and her grandmother were really happy for what they$$),
    ('36998', 6, $$had become. At times they could remember the old days. Later, Lindiwe got married to a God fearing person. Her grandmother was able to see her great grand children. She died a very happy person at the age of 89.$$),
    ('37009', 0, $$Once upon a time the was a boy named Rocxie he loved eating cheese. One morning Rocxie was ready to go to school and his father made breakfast for him and called him for breakfast. Soon the school bus came.$$),
    ('37009', 1, $$Later on Rocxie arrived at school and shouted wait for me and his friends ran to him to ask about the homework they had. Miss Kenny was in class. As miss Kenny said did "everyone write their homework" And everyone said "yes"$$),
    ('37009', 2, $$Miss Kenny said "would someone let us know what did you have to do" Cosmo the bully raised his hand up and said we had to do our homework. Miss Kenny got angry and sent Cosmo to the principals office.$$),
    ('37009', 3, $$But Cosmo did not go to the principals office he just played outside and ate his orange. Rocxie saw that Cosmo was playing outside and told miss Kenny. Miss Kenny went out angry and pulled Cosmo to the principals office.$$),
    ('37009', 4, $$She told the principal Cosmo is a problem at school. So the principal Called Cosmo parents. They came to school and the principal told the story to them and they yelled at Cosmo and the principal suspended him for two weeks.$$),
    ('37009', 5, $$Unfortunately Cosmo was happy it seemed like a holiday to him so he ran out of the school shouting "happy holidays Cosmo" and his parents went out of the school , he's mom celebrated with him. As his father was depressed.$$),
    ('37009', 6, $$Soon it was luch time. Everyone went outside to play and eat. Rocxie and his friends had a great time without Cosmo interrupting them while eating or playing their favorite games.$$),
    ('37009', 7, $$Soon it was science class and miss shimark was in the classroom. As miss shimark said "Everyone today were going to work as partners and discover amazing things so please find a partner and discover amazing things around, you can start now.$$),
    ('37009', 8, $$Miss shimark showed the class a cool experiment on their hands.$$),
    ('37009', 9, $$TWO WEEKS LATER @Cosmo was so tall because he has grown up. No one at school knew that Cosmo was tall. So he stayed at home and told his mom he won't go back until his fine. When his little brother saw him he was shocked.$$),
    ('37009', 10, $$Cosmo gave up because he was not getting better so he went outside and rode his bike. All the school kids laughed at him and some were paying revenge for being such a bully.$$),
    ('37009', 11, $$When he was all better he stopped being a bully because he's scared someone will remind the hole school that he once became a very tall guy. So they went on a school trip to the pool and everyone was happy at the end.😉$$),
    ('37033', 0, $$Hello, nice to meet you! My name is Bohlale. I am nine years old. How old are you?$$),
    ('37033', 1, $$This is my family. I am the youngest and my Gogo is the oldest. I have one brother. He is two years older than me. I also have a sister. She is three years older than my brother. What are the ages of my brother and sister?$$),
    ('37033', 2, $$My siblings are allowed to go to the mountains to collect fruit, and to go to the river. I would love to do those things as well. Everyone always tells me that I am too young, too small, too weak, and not brave enough yet.$$),
    ('37033', 3, $$I wish my family would believe in me! Gogo comes into my room. She kisses me and says, "Goodnight. " Then she whispers in my ear, "Always remember that I believe in you. "$$),
    ('37033', 4, $$I fall asleep. In my dream, I find a message in a bottle. The message is: "If you want to be brave, follow the map to the highest mountain. There you will find a special drink. One sip of that drink will make you the bravest girl in the world. "$$),
    ('37033', 5, $$I am not as wise as my Gogo. I am not as strong as my brother nor as brave as my sister. But if I find this drink, then I will be able to do anything. Help me to follow the map, count 50 steps straight ahead. 1, 2, 3,$$),
    ('37033', 6, $$47, 48, 49, 50 steps! Oh no, a river! How will I make it to the other side? I think I will give up because I cannot swim. Look at that leaf floating on the water! I have got an idea.$$),
    ('37033', 7, $$I can build a raft! Here are five tree branches. How many more branches do I need to build a raft with eleven branches? After building the raft, I can cross the river without swimming. Where will I go next?$$),
    ('37033', 8, $$After 100 steps, I think am lost! Where is the mountain? I will never find the way to the highest mountain. I think I have to give up because I am too small.$$),
    ('37033', 9, $$The giraffe can see the mountain because it is very tall. If I climb this tree, I will be as tall as a giraffe! I can see how far away the mountain is.$$),
    ('37033', 10, $$I climb down from the tree. After 200 steps, I am at the foot of the highest mountain. There is a cave, with scary eyes looking at me! I think I will give up because I am afraid.$$),
    ('37033', 11, $$Look again carefully, those scary eyes are only fireflies. The fireflies could help to guide me through the cave to the top of the mountain.$$),
    ('37033', 12, $$Here I am at the top of the mountain! How many steps did I walk in total? I can see the special drink of bravery! I am going to drink it now.$$),
    ('37033', 13, $$"Good mooooorning! " says Gogo. I wake up suddenly! "Gogo, I had a dream. " I tell Gogo about the message and my journey. "I am still not as wise as you. I am still not as strong as my brother nor as brave as my sister. "$$),
    ('37033', 14, $$Gogo smiles and says, "Are you telling me that you are not brave enough? How did you get to the highest mountain? How did you walk through the cave? You do not need that special drink, because you ARE brave! "$$),
    ('37033', 15, $$Questions 1. How many siblings does Bohlale have?@2. What was in the bottle in her dream?@3. How did she cross the river?@4. Which animal gave her the idea to climb a tree?@5. What did she see in the cave?@6. What did she find on top of the mountain?$$),
    ('37036', 0, $$This is Thato. He is at school in Siyabuswa, South Africa. He is the tallest in his class.$$),
    ('37036', 1, $$Thato lives with his older sister in a friendly neighbourhood. His sister's name is Ntombi.$$),
    ('37036', 2, $$Ntombi is not feeling well today. She cannot go out for groceries, so Thato will have to help. Ntombi gives Thato a list and tells him where to go.$$),
    ('37036', 3, $$Thato's List:@1 bottle of water from the well,@2 bags of flour from the farmer,@3 loaves of bread from the shop,@4 eggs from Junior's Gogo,@5 bunches of herbs from the garden.$$),
    ('37036', 4, $$The first stop on his way is to get water. He needs a bucket and a rope to get water from the well. He can use the shortest rope to reach the water. Which one is the shortest rope?$$),
    ('37036', 5, $$Thato pours the water into his bottle. Now he has to get the flour from the farmer. The farmer is the father of his best friend, Lethabo.$$),
    ('37036', 6, $$The farmer welcomes Thato. He is trying to catch a chicken for supper. He asks Thato to help him to catch a big chicken. Which chicken should Thato catch?$$),
    ('37036', 7, $$Thato is very skilled. He catches the biggest chicken quickly.$$),
    ('37036', 8, $$The farmer gives him two bags of flour.$$),
    ('37036', 9, $$Next stop on Thato's journey is the spaza shop. He has to buy the bread there. "How much bread should I buy? One loaf? " wonders Thato as he checks his shopping list.$$),
    ('37036', 10, $$There are only three loaves left at the shop! One loaf is small, one loaf is large, and one loaf is medium. Thato takes all three loaves.$$),
    ('37036', 11, $$Thato goes to Junior's Gogo to get eggs. Gogo says that Thato can have two eggs for free.@Which box should he take?$$),
    ('37036', 12, $$Thato goes to the garden to collect herbs. There are a lot of plants and he has to look carefully to cut the right herbs. He picks five bunches.$$),
    ('37036', 13, $$Thato carries his groceries in two bags. Which bag is the bigger of the two?$$),
    ('37036', 14, $$Thato arrives home with the groceries. "One bottle of water, two bags of flour, three loaves of bread, six eggs, and five bunches of herbs," counts Thato. How many things altogether?$$),
    ('37036', 15, $$Ntombi is proud of Thato. He got everything on the list, and two extra eggs! Ntombi is feeling better. "Let us make supper," she says to her little brother.$$),
    ('37096', 0, $$It was a hot summer afternoon and a very thirsty crow. was flying above the ground$$),
    ('37096', 1, $$Looking for some water to quench his thirst.$$),
    ('37096', 2, $$All his search went in vain.$$),
    ('37096', 3, $$The sun' s heat had dried up all the water and there was not a drop of water.to be found anywhere.$$),
    ('37096', 4, $$after a long search. The crow finally spotted an abandoned pitcher under a tree.$$),
    ('37096', 5, $$He flew down to it.$$),
    ('37096', 6, $$and was delighted to see some water.still left in the pitcher.$$),
    ('37096', 7, $$But the crow could not reach it's beak to the water all the way down to the bottom of the pitcher.$$),
    ('37096', 8, $$He was sad because he had flown very far to finally find some water.but could not reach the water lying at the bottom of the pitcher.$$),
    ('37096', 9, $$However , he did not give up his hopes of getting the water. He looked around. to see if it could solve this problem somehow.$$),
    ('37096', 10, $$Just then he spotted many pebbles.lying nearby the pitcher. He thought for a while.$$),
    ('37096', 11, $$and a brilliant idea struck his mind.$$),
    ('37096', 12, $$He hurriedly started picking up the pebbles and the dropped them into the pitcher one by one. very soon , the pebbles dicplaced the water at the bottom of the pitcher .$$),
    ('37096', 13, $$and the water slowly sterted raising up the pitcher. So the crow continued dropping the pebbles. and soon the water rose .$$),
    ('37096', 14, $$to the mouth of the pitcher. The crow gulped the water to his content and quenched his thirst. The smart crow was all refreshed and happy.$$),
    ('37096', 15, $$He flew back to the sky. leaving behind a lesson that. " Where there is a will , there is a way ".$$),
    ('37096', 16, $$if you have a positive attitude and if you think through with an open mind you can resolve most of the problems that come in your way.$$),
    ('37129', 0, $$One day while I was sitting in class, I looked through the window and saw a big brown eagle fly past. The eagle's wings were wide open but the wings weren't flapping. This made me curious. I wanted to know more about flying.$$),
    ('37129', 1, $$Maybe birds influenced the invention of airplanes. They both have wings. I wish I could fly, but I do not have wings. I went to the library to find books about airplanes. I wanted to know how they fly.$$),
    ('37129', 2, $$I saw pictures of different flying machines. Some machines had engines, some did not. I saw a hang glider and a parachute. I saw a rocket, a helicopter, a zeppelin, hot air balloons, and some very old airplanes. Ones you could find in museums.$$),
    ('37129', 3, $$How does an airplane fly? Most modern airplanes are powered by jet engines. Jet engines move an airplane forward very fast. That makes the air flow very fast over the airplane's wings. The wings push the air back towards the ground. That causes an upward pressure or force. The upward force holds an airplane in the sky.$$),
    ('37129', 4, $$The closest thing I can do to flying, is in an airplane. Have you ever been in an airplane? I have always dreamed of flying in a big airliner. My teacher told us that we can make our wishes come true just by closing our eyes and imagining.$$),
    ('37129', 5, $$I am your pilot. I am the captain of this aeroplane. Please fasten your seatbelt and prepare to take off from the ground. Clear the runway, I am starting the jet engines!$$),
    ('37129', 6, $$You are a passenger sitting at the window seat. We are speeding along the runway. We are taking off from the airport. The airplane's engines and wings push us into the air. We will fly higher than any bird.$$),
    ('37129', 7, $$My teacher said we can do anything in our imagination. She said we can be whatever we want to be, or do anything we want in our minds Where would you like to fly to?$$),
    ('37137', 0, $$It was the unusually hot summer holidays. Nomfundo and her family were visiting their relatives in Durban. Inside the house it was as hot as the sun itself. After lunch, Nomfundo took her book and went to cool down at the forest near the house.$$),
    ('37137', 1, $$The shade of the two tallest trees gave her enough shade to stay there for a while. There was nothing but the sound of birds. How peaceful!$$),
    ('37137', 2, $$Suddenly, Nomfundo felt something hit her head. "What could that be? " She saw a tiny book next to her. She thought it was her imagination. "I only brought one book here, where is this one coming from? " She looked up the tree, around the tree but did not see anyone.$$),
    ('37137', 3, $$Then she saw the tiniest animal looking down at her. It was a dormouse, a rare and very shy kind of mouse made completely of fur. They are only found in Asia, Europe and Africa.$$),
    ('37137', 4, $$Nomfundo looked up again, and this time she saw the dormouse's nose peeping through the branches. "Hello, I'm Nomfundo. Have you lost something? " Nomfundo asked the dormouse. The small furry rodent squealed in fright and hid behind a leaf. Then the dormouse moved forward again and spoke with a timid voice, "Hello, I'm Bushy. I lost my book. "$$),
    ('37137', 5, $$"I was reading when suddenly a wind blew up," explained Bushy. "I will return your book to you," said Nomfundo. "How? You are down there and I am up here," replied Bushy. But Nomfundo was already running home! She had an idea.$$),
    ('37137', 6, $$Nomfundo went to get the helium balloons that her little brother got for his birthday. She ran back to the forest with the balloons and tied them on a string, around her waist. She floated up the tree. "Welcome to the forest canopy," squealed an excited Bushy.$$),
    ('37137', 7, $$Nomfundo gave the tiny book to Bushy. As a token of friendship, Nomfundo took off one of her ribbons and presented it to Bushy. Bushy tied the ribbon on her tail and the two were friends from that moment. "Come, let's explore the forest canopy," said Bushy.$$),
    ('37137', 8, $$"We must go quietly here, the fruit bat is asleep," whispered Bushy. Bats search for food at night and sleep during the day. They sleep high up in the trees to stay safe from predators.$$),
    ('37137', 9, $$Next, they came across a colourful frog. "Hello Benji, how are you? " Bushy asked the frog. Benji was surprised to see a human in the tree tops! Nomfundo was surprised to see a frog up there! Tree frogs live most of their lives in trees.$$),
    ('37137', 10, $$Suddenly, Nomfundo heard a loud crying sound! It was a bird calling the dormouse. "There's a human! Why is she here? " squawked the Hornbill. "Nomfundo is my friend from the world on the ground," replied Bushy. "Please don't be afraid," said Nomfundo, holding out her hand.$$),
    ('37137', 11, $$The animals welcomed Nomfundo and shared their food with her. But the day is coming to an end, and Nomfundo must leave her friends. She will return to the ground feeling very happy. What a good day she had!$$),
    ('37155', 0, $$Oscar is a little goat. He lives on a farm. He is very brave and adventurous. In his herd there are 20 goats, including Oscar.$$),
    ('37155', 1, $$A herd of 20 cattle live next to the goats. Oscar's best friend is a cow called Shola. One day, Oscar and Shola decide to make friendship bracelets. "Let us make a bracelet for everyone," says Shola. "The bracelets will be a sign of our friendship," agrees Oscar.$$),
    ('37155', 2, $$Oscar and Shola divide the work of making bracelets equally. They each make 20 bracelets. Each bracelet has 1 piece of red wool and 1 piece of blue wool. How many pieces of red and blue wool did they use altogether?$$),
    ('37155', 3, $$Everyone loves the friendship bracelets. The 40 friends are happy together. Then, suddenly, the cattle disappear! Nobody knows what happened. Only half of the animals remain. Oscar decides to search for Shola and the rest of her herd.$$),
    ('37155', 4, $$Oscar sets off on his journey. He comes to a gap in the ground. The gap is too wide to jump over. It is 1 meter wide. He finds some branches that he can use as a bridge. The branches are 150 centimeters long. Will they be long enough?$$),
    ('37155', 5, $$Oscar lays the branches next to each other, and walks across the gap. He is relieved when he reaches the other side! He continues to walk and walk. The day is hot and he becomes very thirsty.$$),
    ('37155', 6, $$Oscar searches for water. He finally sees a river and rushes over to it. The rocks are slippery and Oscar slips and slides! He falls onto a big rock just above the water. He nearly slips into the river.$$),
    ('37155', 7, $$There is a huge crocodile in the river below! Oscar screams for help. He screams until he sees someone coming. It is a cow. The cow shouts, "I will fetch a rope and some friends to help you! "$$),
    ('37155', 8, $$When the cow returns, she throws a rope and Oscar just manages to catch it. The rope is made of pieces of colourful wool. The rope is a little too short. Oscar ties his friendship bracelet to the end of the rope. Now it is long enough.$$),
    ('37155', 9, $$"Hold on tight and we will pull you up," says the cow. Oscar is soon on the river bank. He goes to thank the other cattle and sees his best friend! They are overjoyed and hug each other. Oscar has many questions about what happened.$$),
    ('37155', 10, $$"We wondered away from the farm. We were grazing and a wild dog chased us. We ran for our lives! " says Shola. "We ran so fast and so far that we could not find our way back to the farm. We missed you all! " she adds.$$),
    ('37155', 11, $$Oscar, Shola, and 19 cattle return to the farm. The 19 goats are overjoyed and all the friends are reunited. They are a group of 40 friends again.$$),
    ('37186', 0, $$We are friends and love to play with each other, and fidgets.$$),
    ('37186', 1, $$We must take care of each other!$$),
    ('37186', 2, $$Friends help you$$),
    ('37186', 3, $$Friends should not fight.$$),
    ('37186', 4, $$Friends should not tease$$),
    ('37186', 5, $$Friendships can't break$$),
    ('37186', 6, $$! FRIENDS ARE FIDGETING!$$),
    ('37208', 0, $$Hold an adult's or a friend's hand when you cross the road.$$),
    ('37208', 1, $$Look both ways before crossing. Look right, look left, and look right again before you cross.$$),
    ('37208', 2, $$Do not run or play on the road. You can get hit by cars.$$),
    ('37208', 3, $$You should not talk to people you do not know. Strangers can be dangerous.$$),
    ('37208', 4, $$Do not be afraid to say "no" if a stranger asks you to do something.$$),
    ('37208', 5, $$Matches, lighters, and candles are tools, not toys.$$),
    ('37208', 6, $$Do not play with them. You can get burned.$$),
    ('37208', 7, $$Do not play with knives, scissors, and other sharp objects. You could hurt yourself.$$),
    ('37208', 8, $$Always sleep inside a bed net. This protects you from mosquitoes and nasty diseases like malaria.$$),
